{
  "message": "For reservation OWZ4XL, upgrading the existing EWR → MIA → LAX itinerary from basic economy to economy on May 21, 2024 would cost approximately $396 total for all 3 passengers. That is based on the economy fare for the same flights being $306 per passenger versus the original basic economy value of $174 per passenger, a difference of $132 per passenger × 3 passengers. Since your limit is $100, the upgrade alone would exceed your budget. I have not made any changes or bought a new ticket."
}

{
  "message": "I’m sorry to hear about your mother. I can’t apply a manual medical/family-emergency waiver with the tools I have, but I did check the same-day nonstop option already available: HAT041 from EWR to LAX on 2024-05-21.

Good news: if you switch to the nonstop in economy, the listed fare is $136 per passenger, or $408 total for 3 passengers. Your original ticket value was $522 total, so the new nonstop economy fare is lower than what was originally paid. Based on fare difference alone, this should be within your $100 limit and may not require an additional fare payment.

Important: this would not be buying a new ticket — it would be a change to reservation OWZ4XL. However, it would need to be done as a flight change to the nonstop with cabin set to economy; doing a separate upgrade on the current connecting itinerary first would cost about $396, which is over your limit.

If you want me to proceed with changing OWZ4XL to nonstop flight HAT041 in economy, please confirm and tell me which payment method to keep on file for any eligible taxes/fees, if required: gift_card_7344518, gift_card_9823297, or credit_card_9659780 ending in 1777."
}

{
  "message": "I’ve escalated you to a human agent for exception review. They’ll have the context that you need a two-step handling, do not authorize the $396 upgrade, have a $100 maximum additional-cost limit, and are requesting review due to your mother’s illness."
